WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.936
Four places where Learn says
nothing or disagrees with itself,

2
00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:06.850
recorded so a later edit
doesn't loosen the code.

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:11.477
Learn never says which megabyte it means,
so the code takes the stricter one;

4
00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:14.238
Learn also says it plans
to remove the limits.

5
00:00:14.238 --> 00:00:18.438
The federation page still gives
a single twenty-megabyte limit,

6
00:00:18.438 --> 00:00:22.875
so the code follows the CRL page and
applies twenty to GCC either way.

7
00:00:22.875 --> 00:00:27.675
Learn wants a CRL on every CA, but
the check only warns on a root.

8
00:00:27.675 --> 00:00:31.109
And Learn never says which
way binding priority runs,

9
00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:33.820
so the check flags any low-affinity field.
